WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.139
Have you ever heard of Erbil?

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:13.840
Despite threats from Baghdad, it seems probable
that geography students will soon have to

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.410
learn the name of this capital city as well
as its new country: Iraqi Kurdistan.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.810
The 25th of September this year was a historical
moment for the more than 5 million Kurds who

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.859
currently live in this autonomous community
in the north of Iraq.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:31.679
And why was this?

00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:36.300
Well, that’s because after decades of unfulfilled
promises and ethnic repression, they had the

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.129
opportunity to vote in a referendum organized
by the Regional Government of Kurdistan.

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:47.390
Since 2005, and according to the Constitution
of Iraq, Kurdistan is an autonomous region...

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:52.010
but this area worked, essentially, almost
as a totally independent country.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:57.360
And the result of this was that the population
really wanted to be fully independent.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:04.760
The day of the referendum, Kurds show up en-mass
at the polling stations.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.140
Even speakers at mosques encouraged voters
to go to the polls.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.939
Well, the final results showed the referendum
was a complete success…

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:15.159
More than 7 out of every 10 Kurds went to
vote.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:17.880
That almost 3.1 million votes.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.710
The victory was overwhelming for those who
supported independence, obtaining 92.73% of

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:25.710
the vote.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.000
And you know what, this triumph is totally
understandable, because we are talking about

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.760
some of the most ill-treated people in history.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.100
And that’s even though the Kurds are, according
to many experts, the most ancient people in

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:42.799
the entire region.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:46.659
It is estimated that their culture, their
language, theirs rituals, essentially everything

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:50.859
that could define them, have been in this
part of the world (Upper Mesopotamia) for

00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:53.070
more than 4,000 years...

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.509
In fact, many of these experts consider the
city centre of Erbil, the capital, as the

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:02.600
oldest human settlement to be continuously
inhabited on the planet.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:10.800
In other words, the Kurds are older than the
Persians or the Arabs.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.900
However, they have suffered from all kinds
of persecution.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.250
See, the total number of Kurds is around 30
million, spread across, mainly, four countries:

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.420
Turkey, Iran, Syria and Iraq.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.110
Well, in all these places the Kurds have suffered
the consequences of nationalism that has tried

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.220
to make them disappear as a community.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:32.470
They have tried to end their culture, their
language, as well as trying to close down

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.550
their media outlets.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:39.690
Between 1986 and 1989, Saddam Hussein launched
the “Anfal Campaign” and estimations are

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.650
that between 50,000 and 180,000 Kurds died
as a result of this campaign.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:47.680
And as you might imagine, this cannot be easily
forgotten.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.450
“My grandfather had a good sense of humor.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.940
He used to say he was born a Kurd, in a free
country.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.000
Then the Ottomans arrived and said to my grandfather,
"You're Ottoman," [...] At the fall of the

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.450
Ottoman Empire, he became Turkish.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.440
The Turks left and he became a Kurd again.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.600
[...] Then the British arrived, so my grandfather
became a subject of His Gracious Majesty.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.320
The British invented Iraq, so my grandfather
became Iraqi, but [...] to his dying breath

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.980
he was never proud of being Iraqi.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.870
Hiner Saleem, “My father's rifle : a childhood
in Kurdistan”.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.380
Considering the history, it is no surprise
that the Kurds want, once and for all, to

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.150
make the dream of having their own state come
true.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.960
And if we add up the fact that the Iraqi Kurdistan
is quite a rich area in terms of oil and natural

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:28.780
gas (as well as fresh water, by the way) we
can understand even more why they want independance.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.571
So, to sum up, the Kurds want, and are able,
to build their own country.

00:03:30.571 --> 00:03:38.940
And it is beneficial for them, so, well, they
did that.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.150
THE REFERENDUM

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.150
As we have said, Kurdistan is almost an independent
country already…

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:51.710
they even have their own army of more than
200,000 soldiers: the Peshmerga, who have

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.200
(by the way) been the main defiance to Islamic
State in Iraq.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.850
Do bear this in mind because the government
of Kurdistan is a close ally of Washington.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.150
Maybe their most loyal ally in the area actually.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:06.050
Because of this, the US has trained, financed
and armed their army.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:10.800
Some even say that the Kurds are as pro-American
as Texans!

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:20.109
So, after many difficult years of intense
fighting against Islamic State, it has been

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:23.580
clear for the Kurds that there are almost
no advantages in remaining in Iraq.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.229
And the government of Erbil took advantage
of these battles to integrate Kurd areas into

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:29.389
their political space.

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:33.930
For example there is the province of Kirkuk,
who had a majority of Kurds but was not within

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.949
the autonomous region of Kurdistan.

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:40.020
Kirkuk is something of a “crown jewel”
and one of the main reasons for conflict with

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.230
the Iraqi government, who by the way has not
hesitated to send their troops over to recover

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.230
this settlement.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:49.169
“Iraqi Forces Sweep Into Kirkuk, Checking
Kurdish Independence Drive”

00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:51.150
So why is this territory so valuable?

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.330
Well, that’s Because Kirkuk is the province
that contains the most oil in Kurdistan...

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.930
In fact, it is estimated that around 10% of
all Iraqi oil reserves are concentrated here,

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:07.610
in Kirkuk, and nobody wants to let them go...

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:12.349
In 2007, a referendum should have been conducted
to incorporate (or not) the Autonomous Region

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:15.350
of Kurdistan… but voting never took place.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:19.310
So when the Peshmerga occupied the city in
order to protect it from Islamic State since

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:24.690
the Iraqi army had literally run away… the
Kurd Government had, de facto, annexed the

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.690
territory.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:30.330
So, with these conditions and with constant
negotiations between Baghdad and Erbil (and

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:35.139
with a growing disconnect between both territories)
they eventually got to the referendum.

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:39.530
“This is the first time in history that
the people of Kurdistan will freely decide

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.530
their future.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.409
After that we will start talks with Baghdad,
to reach an agreement over borders, water

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:45.409
and oil”.

00:05:45.409 --> 00:05:47.540
Mr Barzani, president of Iraqi Kurdistan.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:52.729
Now, the government of Iraq opposed this referendum
in every way and the Constitutional Court

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:54.689
of Iraq even outlawed it.

00:05:54.689 --> 00:05:58.199
Parliament asked for many things including:
the withdrawal of diplomatic representation

00:05:58.199 --> 00:06:01.169
in Erbil, a border closure, and even army
deployment…

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:06.320
In Kirkuk there was also prosecution of the
organizers of the referendum and, of course,

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.190
parliament tried their best to remain in control
of all the oil.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:14.259
But...even with this kind of action by the
Iraqi government, the Kurds didn’t really

00:06:14.259 --> 00:06:15.379
care.

00:06:15.379 --> 00:06:22.400
And that’s only logical, because despite
the progress of the Iraqi army, &nbsp;the risk

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:27.300
for Kurdistan is probably not in Iraq, but
rather is with the international community.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.419
You see, Turkey and Iran don't even want to
hear about an independent Kurdistan.

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:36.099
That might give the Kurds in their territories
an idea to replicate this success.

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:40.340
Turkey, for instance, has been at war with
the Kurds for decades, but that’s a story

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:41.340
for another day...

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:46.900
The thing is these countries have allied with
Iraq to defy the referendum:

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.830
Turkey’s military has confirmed that Turkey
and Iraq will conduct joint military drills

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:56.379
in Turkey, along an area bordering Iraq’s
semi-autonomous Kurdish region.

00:06:56.379 --> 00:07:02.539
Iran’s semi-official ISNA news agency reported
that on Sunday that the Supreme National Security

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:08.129
Council closed Iranian airspace to the Iraqi
Kurdish area at the request of the central

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:09.520
government in Baghdad.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.810
And no, it's not just about the possibility
of conflict...

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:16.279
After all, it is likely to be the result of
fear tactics (which are very usual in this

00:07:16.279 --> 00:07:19.089
kind of situations) and they rarely work,
by the way.

00:07:19.089 --> 00:07:22.999
Remember Kurdistan is a close ally of the
USA and they have an experienced and well

00:07:22.999 --> 00:07:23.999
trained army...

00:07:23.999 --> 00:07:28.389
No, the bigger issue might be that Kurdistan
needs their neighbours...

00:07:28.389 --> 00:07:33.289
This territory is landlocked and they are
very dependent on Turkey: both to export their

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:36.249
oil to and to import anything they might need...

00:07:36.249 --> 00:07:40.580
So, a trade blockade would be a serious threat
for this territory.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:46.729
“The KRG’s economy depends on one pipeline
that sells oil to international markets and

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:48.009
the pipeline goes through Turkey.

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:52.819
You shut down that pipeline, you choke the
Kurdish economy,” Bilal Wahab, analyst at

00:07:52.819 --> 00:07:55.259
the Washington Institute for Near East Policy.

00:07:55.259 --> 00:07:57.530
But there is more to it than their neighbours.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.309
Nobody wants any more tension with this part
of the world so, .internationally speaking,

00:08:01.309 --> 00:08:03.439
the referendum didn´t get much support.

00:08:03.439 --> 00:08:07.939
The US has opposed it, and Antonio Guterres,
Secretary General of the UN has described

00:08:07.939 --> 00:08:10.439
it as “dangerous and potentially disruptive”.

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:14.069
Today, only Israel clearly supports the independence
of this country.

00:08:14.069 --> 00:08:16.509
The future doesn't look very good then, does
it?

00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:21.159
Well, wait, because despite all this, it is
likely that Kurdistan will achieve independence

00:08:21.159 --> 00:08:22.460
sooner or later...

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:35.659
THE REASONS FOR A NEW COUNTRY

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:40.090
Iraqi Kurdistan has many issues, however they
have managed to become the region that functions

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.440
the best in Iraq.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.000
They are the safest and wealthiest area.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.839
“I’ve been to Iraqi Kurdistan a number
of times.

00:08:46.839 --> 00:08:51.350
It’s safer than Kansas [...] If you’re
coming from Baghdad or Mosul, it’s practically

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.350
Switzerland”.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.350
Michael J. Totten.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.350
American journalist.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:59.230
Check this out: In 2014, before the IS offensive,
this region was turning into the most relevant

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:04.500
financial and tourist spot in Iraq - an oasis
for many businessmen, both local and foreign...

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.899
Skyscrapers, malls, and mansions, were spreading
like mushrooms after the rain…

00:09:07.899 --> 00:09:10.900
That was until the war broke out in Iraq against
the Islamic State.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.170
Then, most of this development had to stop.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:18.770
Now, after some awful years of war, in 2017
the numbers are bouncing back…

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.940
And remember that this area is oil rich.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:25.170
Some estimations calculate the oil reserves
of Kurdistan as 45 billion barrels!

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:30.480
To put it into words, Kurdistan would be among
the 15 oil richest countries on Earth.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.720
And this is in a country with little more
than 5 million inhabitants.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.720
But there is still so much more…

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.860
Iraq´s Kurdistan is quite business friendly.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.970
Indeed, they like private initiatives…

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.940
something uncommon in this part of the globe.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.560
Taxes are also attractive and bureaucracy
is not excessive either.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.389
Unfortunately though, there is still plenty
of corruption.

00:09:49.389 --> 00:09:54.070
“The Kurdistan Government will do its best
to help the private sector and have them invest

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.070
here.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:59.420
[...] I invite all local and foreign investors
here to take advantage of our laws and offers,

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.420
and invest”.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.839
Masoud Barzani, president of Iraqi Kurdistan.

00:10:02.839 --> 00:10:07.740
The thing is that this region has enough going
for it to make Kurdistan a prosperous country...

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.130
They have fertile land, high levels of safety,
and natural resources.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:16.910
Further, their geographical location is beneficial:
a place between Turkey, Iran and Iraq.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.709
But, on top of that: This new country is only…

00:10:19.709 --> 00:10:20.709
well… fair...

00:10:20.709 --> 00:10:24.870
The Kurd people, and especially Iraqi Kurds
have been deported, attacked with chemical

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:29.440
weapons, and have suffered all sorts of social
engineering in order to strangle their culture.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.730
And now they have an opportunity to build
their own country.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:36.730
Further, the rest of us could also benefit
from a more moderate, prosperous and free

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.350
country than the ones around it...

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:40.829
The Middle East would certainly be better
for it.

00:10:40.829 --> 00:10:43.850
Are what about the problems in today's Iraqi
Kurdistan, are there any?

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:49.399
Well, of course there are, but that is no
excuse to not make this happen.

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:54.290
First, because these problems exist now (with
them still being a part of Iraq), and second:

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:58.580
because they are less serious problems than
the ones in the rest of the country.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:10:59.580
So, is there corruption?

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:00.580
Yes, totally.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.580
Is there oil dependency?

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.580
Yes indeed.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.580
Debt?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.580
Oh yes, that too...

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.140
But this is totally normal in this part of
the world…

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.120
The rest of Iraq is in a much worse situation
for sure.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.470
Well, anyway, we just wish that Baghdad's
response does not turn this situation into

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:14.470
a military conflict.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:19.259
That would be a terrible scenario for everyone,
and would be also one of those situations

00:11:19.259 --> 00:11:22.410
where political interests prevailed above
the people’s.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:26.790
But now it’s time for your opinion: do you
support the independence of Kurdistan?

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.279
Well, leave your answer in the comments as
well as in the survey.

